{"index": 11, "prompt_id": "planning-dependencies", "response": "Sure! Here's a six-step dependency-aware plan to move your website to a new domain without unnecessary downtime:\n\n---\n\n**Step 1: Plan and Design the Site**\n\n- Choose a new domain name and ensure it is unique and easy to remember.\n- Design a clean, professional website with a clear header, header, and content.\n- Plan for a minimum 10-15 minutes of downtime before moving.\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Set Up DNS**\n\n- Use a DNS service (like GoDense, Namecheap, or a free DNS service) to create a new DNS record for your new domain.\n- Test the DNS settings to ensure they point to the correct subnet and DNS name.\n- Schedule DNS changes to avoid downtime.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Backup the Site**\n\n- Create a copy of your current site (easily available online or in a local drive) to back up.\n- Test the site to ensure it works before moving.\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: TLS and Security**\n\n- Use a secure TLS (like Let's Transform or OpenWrap) to secure your website.\n- Ensure all files are protected with strong hashes", "result_sha256": "883a133d24ff5e036c6b07f7ff9b5bc8fc4ba4266da850a4d83b63f490bb4ce7", "stage": "prompt-result-complete"}
